{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: cut SKILL.md to the working loop and point each step at its command.\n\nWhy. SKILL.md is 5,200 words of normative prose that agents re-read about 1,900 times across 52 local sessions, and AGENTS.md another 1,500 words; together with the reference pages they are what \"checking the rules\" costs. Once the step commands land (request: step commands and gs work --next), the shape of each act lives in the CLI and its refusals, so the skill can say what to do and which command does it, and the reasoning can live where it is read once.\n\nOutcome. SKILL.md becomes the loop: orient, answer every request addressed to you, promise, implement on a worktree, publish the artifact set, request review, review, land, clean up; each step names its gs command and the one or two facts an actor must supply. Rules that are now enforced by a command or the fold are stated once as \"the command refuses X\" rather than explained. Reasoning and history move to docs/concepts pages that the skill links. AGENTS.md step 5 shrinks the same way. Nothing normative is lost: every rule removed from the prose is either enforced by a command, tested, or moved to a linked page, and the head lists that mapping in its commit message.","body":{"branch":"request/skill-to-the-loop","conditions":"1. SKILL.md is under 1,500 words and reads as the working loop with one command per step; AGENTS.md's repository-work section is correspondingly shortened. 2. Every sentence removed is accounted for in the commit message as enforced-by (command or fold rule, with the test that pins it), moved-to (page and section), or dropped-as-redundant, and a reviewer can check the mapping. 3. The docset gate and every runnable example still pass; the skill front matter rests on the artifacts for the commands it describes. 4. Depends on the step-commands request having landed; do not start before that. 5. go test ./... green at the exact head; independent review by codex; ratified; landed on main and pushed.","target_head":"c3cc0e4479f9d0e3a5f04e20ecdcfecdc492ecd9","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}